          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by forming the best three-card hand from the five dealt, or by forcing others to fold.',
          gameplay: "1. **Selection**: Players receive 5 cards and discard 2. 2. **Vying**: Standard Brag betting follows. Players choose to play 'Blind' (without looking at their chosen 3) or 'See'. 3. **Ranks**: Prial > Running Flush > Run > Flush > Pair > High Card.",
          keyRules: [
            'The choice of which three cards to keep is the primary skill element.',
            'Blind players bet half the price of Seeing players.',
            'Equal hands favor the player who remained Blind longer.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "With 5 cards to choose from, you should rarely play a hand that isn't at least a Flush. Look for high pairs or consecutive suit sequences.",
          intermediate: "The 'Hidden' Prial: If you are dealt a pair and two cards of another suit, evaluate if it's better to keep the pair for a safe 'Seeing' bet or gamble on a 'Blind' bet with potentially higher hidden value.",
          advanced: "Discard Tracking: Since every player mucks two cards, 8-16 cards are taken out of play in a 4-8 player game. Track which ranks are most common in your 5 cards to deduce which suits/ranks are depleted in opponents' hands.",
          tips: [
            "Don't fall in love with a low pair; in 5-card Brag, a low pair is a very weak hand.",
            "If you hold a 3 and two wild cards ('Braggers'), you have the top hand (Prial of 3s).",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
